1
00:07:19,201 --> 00:07:20,201
Hi, miss.

2
00:07:21,072 --> 00:07:22,632
How much would it cost
to have one made?

3
00:07:24,035 --> 00:07:25,040
That depends...

4
00:07:25,065 --> 00:07:26,149
How many do you need?

5
00:07:27,834 --> 00:07:28,834
Is that so?

6
00:07:30,754 --> 00:07:31,922
Don’t you have...

7
00:07:32,647 --> 00:07:34,190
a special price for your regulars?

8
00:07:41,890 --> 00:07:43,725
I don’t like being lowballed.

9
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:45,882
If that’s what you want,

10
00:07:46,916 --> 00:07:48,292
then go somewhere else.

11
00:07:52,076 --> 00:07:53,119
Suit yourself.

12
00:07:53,958 --> 00:07:55,668
I just got a big bonus,

13
00:07:56,087 --> 00:07:58,381
and I’ll make sure
to pay you well...

14
00:07:58,762 --> 00:07:59,882
really well.

15
00:09:06,141 --> 00:09:08,435
I don’t kiss customers.

16
00:09:08,764 --> 00:09:10,252
Only the one I love.

17
00:09:10,312 --> 00:09:11,312
Really?

18
00:09:57,651 --> 00:09:58,735
Ah shit.

19
00:10:10,288 --> 00:10:11,748
Ah shit.

20
00:10:28,515 --> 00:10:29,573
Don’t be so loud.

21
00:10:30,266 --> 00:10:31,559
Someone might hear us.

22
00:11:19,566 --> 00:11:20,817
Ah shit.

23
00:11:21,609 --> 00:11:22,609
Shit.

24
00:11:24,019 --> 00:11:25,139
Keep it down.

25
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,450
Hello?

26
00:11:29,284 --> 00:11:30,410
Hello?

27
00:11:30,994 --> 00:11:32,713
Is anyone here?

28
00:11:33,413 --> 00:11:35,533
What kind of tailor shop is this?
There’s nobody here!

29
00:11:36,683 --> 00:11:37,861
Coming!

30
00:11:37,968 --> 00:11:38,968
I’m coming!

31
00:11:38,999 --> 00:11:40,171
Coming!

32
00:11:46,593 --> 00:11:48,052
Just a second, miss!

33
00:11:55,036 --> 00:11:56,454
What do you need?

34
00:11:56,938 --> 00:11:58,358
I’d like to have something tailored.

35
00:11:58,382 --> 00:12:00,565
Okay. Just a moment, please.

36
00:12:18,051 --> 00:12:19,051
Ah!

37
00:12:19,133 --> 00:12:20,259
Can you still fit me in?

38
00:12:20,892 --> 00:12:22,894
We’re already closed.
Please come back tomorrow.

39
00:12:23,146 --> 00:12:25,982
I’ve been walking around
this area for a while.

40
00:12:26,007 --> 00:12:27,927
I’ve been looking for a tailor,
but I couldn’t find one.

41
00:12:27,951 --> 00:12:28,965
Can you please...

42
00:12:29,297 --> 00:12:30,673
make an exception for me?

43
00:12:35,253 --> 00:12:36,515
Alright. Come on in.

44
00:12:37,287 --> 00:12:38,395
Thank you.

45
00:12:47,028 --> 00:12:49,030
What would you like to have tailored?

46
00:12:50,281 --> 00:12:51,658
Uhh...

47
00:12:52,987 --> 00:12:54,341
Coat and pants.

48
00:12:54,719 --> 00:12:55,720
Can you finish them in...

49
00:12:55,745 --> 00:12:56,745
A week?

50
00:12:57,038 --> 00:12:59,457
If it’s just a simple design, I can.

51
00:12:59,869 --> 00:13:01,537
Do you have your own fabric?

52
00:13:02,246 --> 00:13:03,246
Ahh...

53
00:13:03,853 --> 00:13:05,688
Looks like you sell fabric too.

54
00:13:05,713 --> 00:13:07,743
Can I just buy from you instead?

55
00:13:08,174 --> 00:13:09,716
Sure... Sir?

56
00:13:10,419 --> 00:13:11,808
Joel Aguilar.

57
00:13:12,512 --> 00:13:13,512
Just Joel.

58
00:13:13,763 --> 00:13:16,182
No need for formalities.
I’m still young.

59
00:13:16,888 --> 00:13:18,181
I’m Elsie.

60
00:13:24,611 --> 00:13:25,810
Please turn around.

61
00:13:32,694 --> 00:13:34,585
Relaxed fit, or slim fit?

62
00:13:36,322 --> 00:13:37,412
Relaxed fit.

63
00:13:44,794 --> 00:13:46,629
Where will you be using this for?

64
00:13:46,965 --> 00:13:48,007
Your wedding?

65
00:13:49,132 --> 00:13:51,825
No. A business conference.

66
00:13:52,218 --> 00:13:54,596
Wow, you must be doing pretty well.

67
00:13:54,721 --> 00:13:56,192
What are you doing here?

68
00:13:56,899 --> 00:13:58,576
You look like you can
afford branded clothes.

69
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,600
Please face me.

70
00:14:00,541 --> 00:14:01,667
Ah, sorry.

71
00:14:02,749 --> 00:14:03,876
Not really.

72
00:14:04,188 --> 00:14:05,523
It’s just that...

73
00:14:05,567 --> 00:14:07,235
A custom-tailored suit.

74
00:14:07,587 --> 00:14:08,587
Uh...

75
00:14:09,127 --> 00:14:10,587
Fits your body better.

76
00:14:10,612 --> 00:14:12,430
The measurements are more accurate.

77
00:14:57,723 --> 00:14:59,610
You’re pretty tall, Joel.

78
00:15:03,556 --> 00:15:04,620
How much?

79
00:15:06,248 --> 00:15:08,822
Just pay when you come to pick it up.

80
00:15:19,822 --> 00:15:22,033
Alright, sounds good. Thank you.

81
00:15:23,027 --> 00:15:24,028
Thank you.

82
00:15:39,702 --> 00:15:40,787
Elsie!

83
00:15:41,765 --> 00:15:42,765
Elsie!

84
00:15:44,288 --> 00:15:45,380
Elsie!

85
00:15:46,749 --> 00:15:48,001
Oh! Betchay!

86
00:15:48,036 --> 00:15:50,080
Come down for a bit. Let’s talk.

87
00:15:50,331 --> 00:15:51,499
Okay, just a second.

88
00:15:57,212 --> 00:15:58,768
Oh. Betchay.

89
00:15:59,032 --> 00:16:00,162
What brings you here?

90
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,956
Didn’t I already give you a month?

91
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:06,005
Why? Wasn’t that enough?

92
00:16:07,186 --> 00:16:09,647
I was hoping you’d
change you mind, Betchay.

93
00:16:10,661 --> 00:16:12,283
Moving isn’t easy.

94
00:16:12,441 --> 00:16:14,403
Besides, I pay my rent on time.

95
00:16:15,418 --> 00:16:17,378
I’ve been here for so long, Betchay.

96
00:16:18,114 --> 00:16:21,454
I’ve lived here since my
parents were still alive.

97
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:22,593
Also...

98
00:16:22,618 --> 00:16:25,580
This is where our tailoring
shop built its reputation.

99
00:16:26,595 --> 00:16:27,595
Alright.

100
00:16:27,999 --> 00:16:31,252
Buy my house and lot for five million.

101
00:16:31,307 --> 00:16:32,307
Can you afford it?

102
00:16:32,795 --> 00:16:34,922
Come on, Betchay.

103
00:16:35,146 --> 00:16:37,232
Where am I supposed
to get that kind of money?

104
00:16:37,967 --> 00:16:40,678
Elsie, this is my property.

105
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:43,028
I have every right to sell it!

106
00:16:43,167 --> 00:16:44,167
Now,

107
00:16:44,374 --> 00:16:45,641
if you can’t afford to buy it,

108
00:16:45,725 --> 00:16:47,665
that’s not my problem!

109
00:17:14,777 --> 00:17:15,813
Hello, Ma’am.

110
00:17:18,147 --> 00:17:22,871
Yes, would you like to have a pair
of school uniforms tailored?

111
00:17:24,764 --> 00:17:26,599
I’ll give you a discount, ma’am.

112
00:17:26,699 --> 00:17:29,052
No, thanks.
The kids will just use their old ones.

113
00:17:29,143 --> 00:17:30,143
Please.

114
00:17:30,311 --> 00:17:31,618
- Ma’am.
- Bye.

115
00:17:31,696 --> 00:17:32,781
Ma’am? Hello?

116
00:17:33,272 --> 00:17:34,282
Hello, ma’am?

117
00:17:36,186 --> 00:17:37,186
Shit...

118
00:17:45,284 --> 00:17:46,326
Hello.

119
00:17:46,661 --> 00:17:47,661
Miss.

120
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:50,748
Maybe you’d like to have a gown made?

121
00:17:51,287 --> 00:17:53,248
I know you and your husband
have an event coming up, right?

122
00:17:53,272 --> 00:17:55,722
No, I already bought a new one.

123
00:17:55,804 --> 00:17:58,182
I’m in a hurry. Maybe next time.

124
00:18:19,569 --> 00:18:21,446
You look deep in thought.

125
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,483
Oh, it’s you.

126
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:27,034
Ah... I already finished
the suit you ordered.

127
00:18:27,426 --> 00:18:28,595
There’s a fitting room over there.

128
00:18:28,619 --> 00:18:29,860
You can try it on inside.

129
00:18:31,195 --> 00:18:33,441
Okay... I’ll hand it to you, sir.

130
00:19:02,106 --> 00:19:03,607
I’ll help you try it on.

131
00:19:20,046 --> 00:19:21,047
I can manage.

132
00:20:05,675 --> 00:20:06,693
Looks great.

133
00:20:09,553 --> 00:20:10,590
I like it.

134
00:20:13,269 --> 00:20:14,295
How much?

135
00:20:17,786 --> 00:20:18,956
For you,

136
00:20:21,114 --> 00:20:22,807
five thousand is okay.

137
00:20:27,899 --> 00:20:28,899
Um...

138
00:20:38,833 --> 00:20:40,543
Something this well-made...

139
00:20:42,837 --> 00:20:44,174
shouldn’t be lowballed.

140
00:20:51,274 --> 00:20:53,680
I don’t kiss my customers.

141
00:20:54,598 --> 00:20:56,287
Only the one I love.

142
00:24:48,008 --> 00:24:49,243
Thank you.

143
00:25:00,469 --> 00:25:03,430
Doesn’t anyone get mad
when you come home this late?

144
00:25:07,434 --> 00:25:09,645
Are you trying to find out...

145
00:25:09,812 --> 00:25:10,964
if I’m married?

146
00:25:12,273 --> 00:25:13,357
Are you?

147
00:25:14,692 --> 00:25:15,797
What do you think?

148
00:25:16,443 --> 00:25:17,528
Don’t worry.

149
00:25:17,953 --> 00:25:19,189
I’m not the jealous type.

150
00:25:21,033 --> 00:25:22,910
I’m married to my work.

151
00:25:25,160 --> 00:25:26,161
Wow!

152
00:25:26,186 --> 00:25:27,490
No wonder you’re rich.

153
00:25:29,707 --> 00:25:31,058
Not really.

154
00:25:32,427 --> 00:25:33,819
I grew up poor too.

155
00:25:35,579 --> 00:25:40,125
I just got lucky with
my medical supplies import business.

156
00:25:40,761 --> 00:25:42,761
Must be nice to be that lucky.

157
00:25:45,806 --> 00:25:46,807
What about you?

158
00:25:48,309 --> 00:25:49,935
Have you been a tailor for a long time?

159
00:25:51,895 --> 00:25:53,800
Both my parents were tailors.

160
00:25:54,009 --> 00:25:56,608
They worked at a garment factory...

161
00:25:56,859 --> 00:25:58,360
before they started their own shop.

162
00:25:58,654 --> 00:26:00,614
The sewing machine I use

163
00:26:01,340 --> 00:26:02,508
belonged to them.

164
00:26:05,542 --> 00:26:07,736
Have you lived here long?

165
00:26:09,663 --> 00:26:11,624
About 20 years.

166
00:26:12,541 --> 00:26:14,043
I just rent this place.

167
00:26:15,044 --> 00:26:17,570
We were supposed to buy this house, but...

168
00:26:18,291 --> 00:26:20,234
My parents got into an accident.

169
00:26:21,424 --> 00:26:22,676
Both of them

170
00:26:22,740 --> 00:26:24,207
died in the hospital.

171
00:26:27,788 --> 00:26:28,931
So you’re all alone?

172
00:26:30,017 --> 00:26:32,394
You don’t live with anyone?
No siblings?

173
00:26:34,717 --> 00:26:36,434
I’ve been on my own for five years.

174
00:26:37,706 --> 00:26:40,667
I just can’t bring myself to
leave this house because...

175
00:26:41,737 --> 00:26:44,114
it holds so many
memories of my parents.

176
00:26:45,377 --> 00:26:47,978
I just hope I can save
enough to buy it someday.

177
00:26:49,161 --> 00:26:51,747
My landlady wants me out.

178
00:26:52,779 --> 00:26:54,428
She’s putting the property up for sale.

179
00:27:02,347 --> 00:27:04,683
I can help you buy this property.

180
00:27:06,845 --> 00:27:09,379
No, it’s my problem to deal with.

181
00:27:11,433 --> 00:27:12,559
I insist.

182
00:27:14,895 --> 00:27:16,149
Are you sure?

183
00:27:17,351 --> 00:27:20,685
I wouldn’t offer if
I couldn’t afford it.

184
00:27:22,959 --> 00:27:24,461
First thing tomorrow.

185
00:27:24,568 --> 00:27:26,528
I’ll talk to my landlady.

186
00:27:27,282 --> 00:27:28,282
Thank you.

187
00:27:28,826 --> 00:27:29,910
Thank you so much.

188
00:27:30,619 --> 00:27:31,787
There’s one condition.

189
00:27:33,826 --> 00:27:35,369
It’s my pleasure.

190
00:27:54,077 --> 00:27:55,174
Really, Elsie?

191
00:27:55,342 --> 00:27:56,742
You’re not pulling my leg, are you?

192
00:27:57,146 --> 00:27:58,772
Of course not, Betchay.

193
00:27:58,822 --> 00:28:00,740
Before this week is over,

194
00:28:00,793 --> 00:28:02,410
you’ll have your five million.

195
00:28:02,598 --> 00:28:03,598
Just...

196
00:28:04,237 --> 00:28:06,364
Get the deed of sale ready.

197
00:28:07,694 --> 00:28:08,694
Alright.

198
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:10,066
I’ll be back.

199
00:28:14,137 --> 00:28:15,527
Take care, Betchay.

200
00:32:10,483 --> 00:32:13,812
I miss you so much, Joel.
Keep your promise, okay?

201
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:39,744
How have you been?

202
00:32:41,477 --> 00:32:42,763
I’m not taking any more orders.

203
00:32:48,770 --> 00:32:49,813
Why not?

204
00:32:50,313 --> 00:32:51,513
What, did you win the lottery?

205
00:33:23,182 --> 00:33:25,726
Joel, what took you so long?

206
00:33:26,016 --> 00:33:27,266
I thought...

207
00:33:27,416 --> 00:33:29,084
you’d scammed me.

208
00:33:29,284 --> 00:33:31,203
I just had something to take care of.

209
00:33:32,114 --> 00:33:33,365
Is everything okay?

210
00:33:33,940 --> 00:33:35,567
Nothing, I sorted it out.

211
00:33:36,109 --> 00:33:38,195
So, were you able to
talk to your landlady?

212
00:33:39,386 --> 00:33:41,565
We agreed on five million.

213
00:33:42,783 --> 00:33:43,783
Good.

214
00:33:50,537 --> 00:33:51,537
Joel...

215
00:33:52,167 --> 00:33:54,002
Thank you so, so much.

216
00:33:54,795 --> 00:33:56,254
I never imagined...

217
00:33:56,354 --> 00:33:58,690
this apartment
would become mine.

218
00:33:59,919 --> 00:34:02,422
I know how much this place means to you.

219
00:34:02,636 --> 00:34:03,636
That’s why...

220
00:34:03,678 --> 00:34:06,389
I didn’t hesitate to buy it for you.

221
00:34:07,140 --> 00:34:08,809
Thank you so much, Joel.

222
00:34:09,935 --> 00:34:11,394
You’re such a kind person.

223
00:34:43,468 --> 00:34:44,845
Hi, miss.

224
00:34:45,168 --> 00:34:46,568
Looking to have something tailored?

225
00:34:50,559 --> 00:34:52,102
A Sunday dress.

226
00:34:52,562 --> 00:34:53,647
What style are you after?

227
00:34:53,895 --> 00:34:55,598
I have a portfolio here.

228
00:35:01,111 --> 00:35:02,237
That was fast.

229
00:35:13,071 --> 00:35:14,322
What’s your name?

230
00:35:15,782 --> 00:35:16,782
Jess.

231
00:35:17,983 --> 00:35:20,005
Nice name, unisex.

232
00:35:20,271 --> 00:35:21,873
Jess... What?

233
00:35:22,816 --> 00:35:23,816
Cruz.

234
00:35:27,387 --> 00:35:28,818
I noticed...

235
00:35:29,502 --> 00:35:32,338
Why are most of your customers men?

236
00:35:32,965 --> 00:35:34,466
That’s just a coincidence.

237
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:37,107
Are you single?

238
00:35:38,208 --> 00:35:39,793
In a relationship?

239
00:35:40,692 --> 00:35:41,692
Why?

240
00:35:41,776 --> 00:35:42,986
Just curious.

241
00:35:44,154 --> 00:35:45,808
How young are you?

242
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:48,931
You look about my age.

243
00:35:50,135 --> 00:35:53,096
I’m sorry, miss, but I won’t be able
to make your Sunday dress after all.

244
00:35:53,121 --> 00:35:54,831
I’m not in a hurry.

245
00:35:55,582 --> 00:35:56,583
Don’t worry,

246
00:35:56,875 --> 00:35:58,191
I’ll pay you double.

247
00:36:00,059 --> 00:36:01,438
It’s just that...

248
00:36:02,005 --> 00:36:04,841
You’ve already taken my measurements,
and now you’re telling me that?

249
00:36:18,096 --> 00:36:19,546
Why didn’t you answer?

250
00:36:20,366 --> 00:36:22,479
It’s nothing. Just a service provider.

251
00:36:25,641 --> 00:36:27,165
I’ll be back.

252
00:36:28,507 --> 00:36:29,507
Maybe...

253
00:36:29,532 --> 00:36:30,729
early next week.

254
00:36:33,259 --> 00:36:34,314
Bye for now,

255
00:36:34,667 --> 00:36:35,674
Elsie.

256
00:36:44,901 --> 00:36:46,946
How did she know my name?

257
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:23,570
Why doesn't Joel have
any social media accounts?

258
00:38:14,721 --> 00:38:15,805
Hi.

259
00:38:16,556 --> 00:38:17,849
Hi, Elsie.

260
00:38:18,388 --> 00:38:19,889
Are you done with my dress?

261
00:38:22,441 --> 00:38:23,456
Here.

262
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:30,541
Could you help me with the fitting?

263
00:38:30,566 --> 00:38:32,447
You can just drape it over me.

264
00:38:32,472 --> 00:38:34,307
I’m wearing something thin anyway.

265
00:38:53,927 --> 00:38:55,136
Ow!

266
00:39:00,642 --> 00:39:02,021
What the hell!

267
00:39:02,310 --> 00:39:03,812
Sorry, I didn’t mean to.

268
00:39:03,853 --> 00:39:05,688
I forgot to remove the pin.

269
00:39:05,955 --> 00:39:07,165
Did you do that on purpose?

270
00:39:07,190 --> 00:39:08,817
You did!
You did it on purpose!

271
00:39:08,858 --> 00:39:10,734
Gigi! Stop!

272
00:39:11,998 --> 00:39:13,374
Calm down, will you?

273
00:39:13,822 --> 00:39:15,532
Don’t make a scene here!

274
00:39:15,763 --> 00:39:17,014
You’re stupid.

275
00:39:19,285 --> 00:39:20,285
Gigi!

276
00:39:21,955 --> 00:39:23,581
I’m sorry, but I have to go.

277
00:39:23,855 --> 00:39:25,732
I have to catch up with my daughter.

278
00:39:37,782 --> 00:39:39,579
So she’s Joel’s daughter.

279
00:39:47,689 --> 00:39:48,689
Gigi!

280
00:39:48,995 --> 00:39:50,584
- Gigi!
- What?

281
00:39:50,942 --> 00:39:52,735
What were you doing there?

282
00:39:52,868 --> 00:39:54,620
Shouldn’t you be in school?

283
00:39:55,864 --> 00:39:58,366
Shouldn’t I be asking you the same thing?

284
00:39:58,620 --> 00:40:00,830
What were you doing there, Dad?

285
00:40:01,168 --> 00:40:03,170
Shouldn’t you be at the office?

286
00:40:05,154 --> 00:40:07,385
Did you really think I wouldn’t find out?

287
00:40:07,503 --> 00:40:08,629
Elsie.

288
00:40:08,918 --> 00:40:10,503
That’s her name, right?

289
00:40:11,637 --> 00:40:13,639
So that’s your type now.

290
00:40:15,118 --> 00:40:17,817
- Dad!
- Don’t disrespect her!

291
00:40:17,842 --> 00:40:19,427
She deserves it.

292
00:40:19,512 --> 00:40:22,724
Does she even know your wife’s body
hasn’t even decomposed yet?

293
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:25,185
And you’ve already replaced her.

294
00:40:26,012 --> 00:40:27,346
All this time.

295
00:40:27,729 --> 00:40:30,315
I thought you were still grieving Mom.

296
00:40:31,060 --> 00:40:33,168
Turns out you’ve already
found her replacement?

297
00:40:33,193 --> 00:40:36,447
No one could ever replace
the love I have for your mother.

298
00:40:36,472 --> 00:40:38,269
Congratulations!

299
00:40:38,406 --> 00:40:40,135
Husband of the Year, huh?

300
00:40:43,411 --> 00:40:45,121
I’m not doing anything wrong.

301
00:40:46,122 --> 00:40:47,790
Your mother is gone, Gigi!

302
00:40:48,166 --> 00:40:49,375
I know!

303
00:40:49,626 --> 00:40:51,211
But how I wish,

304
00:40:51,463 --> 00:40:53,506
you died first, instead of her.

305
00:40:55,298 --> 00:40:56,549
That’s what I wish too.

306
00:40:56,970 --> 00:40:58,190
Believe it or not.

307
00:40:58,301 --> 00:41:00,386
You had a choice that day...

308
00:41:00,637 --> 00:41:02,722
but you let Mom die.

309
00:41:03,948 --> 00:41:05,909
So no matter how much
you play the victim...

310
00:41:05,934 --> 00:41:08,058
I’ll never believe you again.

311
00:41:32,335 --> 00:41:34,337
I miss you, Mom.

312
00:41:41,386 --> 00:41:42,386
Hey!

313
00:41:43,388 --> 00:41:44,762
What’s with you?

314
00:41:44,906 --> 00:41:47,797
- Can’t you see someone’s having a moment?
- You’re drinking?

315
00:41:48,226 --> 00:41:50,061
I thought you were supposed to be studying?

316
00:41:50,228 --> 00:41:51,312
Shut up!

317
00:41:56,427 --> 00:41:58,288
You always ruin the moment!

318
00:42:29,819 --> 00:42:33,532
- Wait, your dad might hear us.
- No, it's fine.

319
00:45:09,571 --> 00:45:11,489
I was worried for days.

320
00:45:12,389 --> 00:45:13,588
I thought...

321
00:45:13,844 --> 00:45:15,008
she was your wife.

322
00:45:17,059 --> 00:45:18,978
So her name is Gigi.

323
00:45:19,760 --> 00:45:21,762
She introduced herself differently to me.

324
00:45:23,618 --> 00:45:24,619
Face me.

325
00:45:33,778 --> 00:45:34,974
We’re not okay.

326
00:45:37,455 --> 00:45:38,790
Remember?

327
00:45:39,248 --> 00:45:40,326
When...

328
00:45:41,459 --> 00:45:44,420
I didn’t come by for a few days?

329
00:45:45,922 --> 00:45:47,215
We had a big fight.

330
00:45:49,258 --> 00:45:51,135
I found out that...

331
00:45:51,733 --> 00:45:53,485
she hadn’t been going to school.

332
00:45:55,139 --> 00:45:57,029
She started acting that way after...

333
00:45:58,059 --> 00:46:00,645
her mother died of cancer.

334
00:46:02,688 --> 00:46:03,934
That was three months ago.

335
00:46:04,857 --> 00:46:06,567
Why was she so angry at you?

336
00:46:07,318 --> 00:46:08,402
Well...

337
00:46:08,528 --> 00:46:11,364
When Aileen’s condition
got really bad in the hospital,

338
00:46:13,741 --> 00:46:15,743
I spoke to her doctor.

339
00:46:18,171 --> 00:46:19,479
I told him

340
00:46:20,122 --> 00:46:22,083
not to go through the procedure.

341
00:46:24,794 --> 00:46:27,129
That’s what Aileen wanted.

342
00:46:28,047 --> 00:46:29,298
She made me promise.

343
00:46:29,668 --> 00:46:31,962
She didn’t want to suffer anymore.

344
00:46:35,054 --> 00:46:36,597
She also had a DNR.

345
00:46:37,406 --> 00:46:38,908
Do Not Resuscitate.

346
00:46:41,037 --> 00:46:43,998
Gigi just couldn’t accept that.

347
00:46:47,508 --> 00:46:48,610
I just don’t know.

348
00:46:48,885 --> 00:46:50,117
She’s still young.

349
00:46:51,445 --> 00:46:52,822
Were you two close?

350
00:46:53,498 --> 00:46:55,296
She was much closer to her Mom.

351
00:46:57,076 --> 00:46:58,309
I don’t know.

352
00:46:59,878 --> 00:47:01,839
We just never really got along.

353
00:47:02,665 --> 00:47:04,750
Kids go through phases.

354
00:47:05,209 --> 00:47:07,128
Maybe just try to understand her.

355
00:47:09,380 --> 00:47:11,215
I don’t like seeing you like this.

356
00:47:12,174 --> 00:47:14,218
I don’t want you to be sad.

357
00:51:17,776 --> 00:51:18,776
Oh my god...

358
00:51:19,897 --> 00:51:21,316
Don’t worry.

359
00:51:22,550 --> 00:51:25,061
I’ll help you make things
right with your daughter.

360
00:51:41,652 --> 00:51:44,071
You’ve been coming home late a lot lately.

361
00:51:44,684 --> 00:51:46,353
Is that what a model father does?

362
00:52:20,309 --> 00:52:22,047
Gigi! It’s you.

363
00:52:22,559 --> 00:52:24,173
I was thinking about you.

364
00:52:24,793 --> 00:52:26,587
I wanted to talk to you.

365
00:52:28,449 --> 00:52:31,035
Your dad and I had a heart-to-heart talk.

366
00:52:31,974 --> 00:52:35,101
He opened up about the
tension between you two.

367
00:52:37,238 --> 00:52:39,401
I don’t mean to pry, but...

368
00:52:41,171 --> 00:52:44,130
You can talk to me if you
need someone to listen.

369
00:52:45,566 --> 00:52:48,688
Thanks for your concern,
but that’s not why I’m here.

370
00:52:50,205 --> 00:52:52,874
I came to ask you for a favor.

371
00:52:54,016 --> 00:52:56,769
If it’ll help you and
your dad reconcile,

372
00:52:57,421 --> 00:52:58,717
I’m willing to help.

373
00:52:59,939 --> 00:53:00,939
Kill.

374
00:53:01,192 --> 00:53:02,192
Dad.

375
00:53:02,566 --> 00:53:04,276
I want to get my inheritance now.

376
00:53:06,487 --> 00:53:09,448
And I’ll give you two million
as a down payment.

377
00:53:10,241 --> 00:53:11,459
There’ll be more...

378
00:53:11,951 --> 00:53:14,161
once I get my inheritance after he dies.

379
00:53:15,156 --> 00:53:17,325
You want your own father killed?

380
00:53:21,763 --> 00:53:23,829
You have no idea.

381
00:53:24,338 --> 00:53:26,173
Gigi, how did you end up like this?

382
00:53:26,799 --> 00:53:28,259
Joel is your father!

383
00:53:28,467 --> 00:53:29,468
Come on.

384
00:53:30,240 --> 00:53:32,054
Drop the act.

385
00:53:32,209 --> 00:53:33,919
It’s just the two of us here.

386
00:53:35,074 --> 00:53:36,408
You can be honest.

387
00:53:36,433 --> 00:53:38,692
You’re only after my dad’s money.

388
00:53:41,063 --> 00:53:42,140
I love

389
00:53:42,213 --> 00:53:43,380
your father.

390
00:53:44,900 --> 00:53:46,694
Who are you trying to convince?

391
00:53:46,848 --> 00:53:48,635
Me? Or yourself?

392
00:53:49,898 --> 00:53:51,858
I know women like you.

393
00:53:52,006 --> 00:53:53,086
I’ve seen your type before.

394
00:53:53,826 --> 00:53:56,495
All you care about is money!

395
00:53:57,788 --> 00:54:00,291
Just think about it. Once I pay you,

396
00:54:00,708 --> 00:54:02,584
you’ll be able to renovate this shop.

397
00:54:02,960 --> 00:54:04,295
Don’t you want that?

398
00:54:04,962 --> 00:54:06,380
I won’t do what you’re asking.

399
00:54:06,463 --> 00:54:07,501
Get out.

400
00:54:12,278 --> 00:54:14,914
I got into Dad’s phone last night.

401
00:54:15,731 --> 00:54:17,316
And look what I found!

402
00:54:22,790 --> 00:54:25,424
So you sent Dad a topless photo too!

403
00:54:25,778 --> 00:54:26,923
Wild!

404
00:54:29,992 --> 00:54:31,001
Oops!

405
00:54:31,026 --> 00:54:32,063
Not yet.

406
00:54:34,198 --> 00:54:35,949
If you don’t want this getting out,

407
00:54:36,154 --> 00:54:38,240
do what I want, Elsie.

408
00:54:39,204 --> 00:54:41,081
But I’m feeling generous.

409
00:54:41,206 --> 00:54:44,460
I’ll give you 24 hours
to think about it.

410
00:54:46,045 --> 00:54:47,087
Otherwise...

411
00:54:47,333 --> 00:54:49,031
You’ll be all over the internet.

412
00:55:20,454 --> 00:55:21,934
Ms. Elsie, I need to claim a suit.

413
00:55:32,125 --> 00:55:33,125
Ah...

414
00:55:44,286 --> 00:55:45,957
What’s that? Give it to me!

415
00:55:46,587 --> 00:55:47,922
What’s your problem, miss?

416
00:55:52,027 --> 00:55:53,153
Sorry.

417
00:55:55,155 --> 00:55:56,657
Here’s your suit.

418
00:56:03,497 --> 00:56:04,513
Thanks.

419
00:56:15,226 --> 00:56:16,263
Elsie?

420
00:56:18,345 --> 00:56:19,345
Uh...

421
00:56:23,976 --> 00:56:24,976
Elsie.

422
00:56:25,227 --> 00:56:26,854
What time do you close?

423
00:56:27,938 --> 00:56:29,535
Would you like to have dinner with me?

424
00:56:33,709 --> 00:56:34,750
Are you okay?

425
00:56:36,989 --> 00:56:37,989
Elsie.

426
00:56:39,158 --> 00:56:40,158
Elsie.

427
00:56:40,284 --> 00:56:41,284
Huh?

428
00:56:42,411 --> 00:56:43,537
You’ve been so quiet.

429
00:56:43,562 --> 00:56:44,771
Is something wrong?

430
00:56:48,667 --> 00:56:49,793
Joel.

431
00:56:50,085 --> 00:56:51,295
There’s...

432
00:56:54,548 --> 00:56:57,891
- Hello?
- There’s a problem. We screwed up.

433
00:56:58,635 --> 00:56:59,635
What?

434
00:57:00,179 --> 00:57:04,141
Didn’t I tell you
to prioritize that?

435
00:57:05,142 --> 00:57:06,142
Hang on.

436
00:57:07,394 --> 00:57:10,230
Elsie. I have to go
back to the office.

437
00:57:10,522 --> 00:57:11,565
It’s an emergency.

438
00:57:11,590 --> 00:57:12,633
Want to come with me?

439
00:57:12,718 --> 00:57:14,443
You can tell me about it on the way.

440
00:57:14,943 --> 00:57:16,445
No, it’s okay.

441
00:57:16,653 --> 00:57:18,113
You should take care of work first.

442
00:57:18,161 --> 00:57:20,076
- Go ahead.
- Are you sure?

443
00:57:21,332 --> 00:57:22,333
Alright.

444
00:57:24,328 --> 00:57:26,288
So... What happened?

445
00:57:26,288 --> 00:57:29,249
Didn’t I tell you to take
care of this already?

446
00:57:36,423 --> 00:57:38,135
What do you mean you found another buyer?

447
00:57:38,483 --> 00:57:40,235
We already had a deal, didn’t we?

448
00:57:40,999 --> 00:57:42,750
Well, I have another buyer now.

449
00:57:43,201 --> 00:57:46,162
And they’re willing to
pay me seven million.

450
00:57:46,774 --> 00:57:49,110
We already agreed on five million.

451
00:57:49,938 --> 00:57:51,648
I even have your check with me.

452
00:57:52,271 --> 00:57:54,097
And now you’ve suddenly
changed your mind?

453
00:57:54,150 --> 00:57:55,485
You’re impossible to deal with.

454
00:57:55,651 --> 00:57:58,082
Elsie. You don’t get
to tell me what to do.

455
00:57:58,238 --> 00:58:00,282
We don’t have a contract.

456
00:58:01,647 --> 00:58:02,883
Please, Betchay.

457
00:58:04,076 --> 00:58:05,619
I’ve lived here for so long.

458
00:58:07,371 --> 00:58:12,106
I grew up here with my parents.
Please, I’m begging you.

459
00:58:12,250 --> 00:58:15,112
Please, Betchay. Please.

460
00:58:15,254 --> 00:58:18,006
I own this property.

461
00:58:18,802 --> 00:58:21,692
And my decision is final.

462
00:58:33,939 --> 00:58:35,429
So you’re rich after all.

463
00:58:35,941 --> 00:58:36,942
Imagine,

464
00:58:37,192 --> 00:58:40,352
writing a five million check.

465
00:58:41,755 --> 00:58:43,590
Maybe I should become a tailor too!

466
00:58:44,348 --> 00:58:45,348
Oops!

467
00:58:46,987 --> 00:58:49,030
Could that money have come from Dad?

468
00:58:49,805 --> 00:58:51,390
If I’m not mistaken.

469
00:58:51,415 --> 00:58:53,918
You’re going to ask Dad
for another two million.

470
00:58:53,943 --> 00:58:56,143
So you can outbid your landlady.

471
00:58:57,031 --> 00:58:58,950
I’m not as heartless as you think.

472
00:58:59,450 --> 00:59:00,910
Don’t get me wrong.

473
00:59:01,225 --> 00:59:03,269
I’m not judging you, Elsie.

474
00:59:04,177 --> 00:59:06,305
I know you’re just being practical.

475
00:59:07,529 --> 00:59:08,529
I heard...

476
00:59:08,765 --> 00:59:11,827
The reason you can’t leave this place
is because of your parents.

477
00:59:13,458 --> 00:59:14,751
Aww!

478
00:59:15,439 --> 00:59:16,732
How sweet.

479
00:59:18,734 --> 00:59:20,944
Why do you hate your father so much?

480
00:59:21,918 --> 00:59:24,212
Your mother chose to let go.

481
00:59:24,736 --> 00:59:26,336
That’s what she asked your father to do.

482
00:59:26,923 --> 00:59:29,259
I don’t know what version
of the story you’ve been told.

483
00:59:29,800 --> 00:59:31,802
But don’t play God.

484
00:59:32,247 --> 00:59:34,105
There are a lot of things you don’t know.

485
00:59:34,916 --> 00:59:37,461
Especially about me and Joel.

486
00:59:41,673 --> 00:59:43,549
Fine! Okay.

487
00:59:44,009 --> 00:59:46,595
So you won’t think
I’m completely heartless.

488
00:59:47,554 --> 00:59:49,222
I’ll tell you a secret.

489
00:59:51,683 --> 00:59:53,935
Joel isn’t my biological father.

490
00:59:54,608 --> 00:59:56,819
That DNR issue...

491
00:59:57,357 --> 00:59:59,109
was just the icing on the cake.

492
01:00:03,694 --> 01:00:05,816
Just before Mom died,

493
01:00:06,198 --> 01:00:07,449
she talked to me.

494
01:00:08,659 --> 01:00:09,993
It was just the two of us.

495
01:00:11,246 --> 01:00:12,873
And she told me...

496
01:00:13,664 --> 01:00:16,083
Joel isn’t my real father.

497
01:00:17,334 --> 01:00:20,045
She even showed me our DNA test.

498
01:00:21,254 --> 01:00:23,298
Mom kept it hidden from Dad.

499
01:00:25,976 --> 01:00:29,221
Is that why you’re in such
a hurry to get your inheritance?

500
01:00:29,246 --> 01:00:30,246
Yup!

501
01:00:30,376 --> 01:00:31,376
That’s one.

502
01:00:31,515 --> 01:00:34,476
I’m still more upset
that Mom’s gone.

503
01:00:35,159 --> 01:00:36,159
So...

504
01:00:37,020 --> 01:00:39,648
all those times you ranted at him,

505
01:00:40,800 --> 01:00:41,900
it was all an act?

506
01:00:42,033 --> 01:00:43,321
It worked!

507
01:00:43,568 --> 01:00:44,568
Didn’t it?

508
01:00:44,986 --> 01:00:47,531
I just played the part
of an angry teenager.

509
01:00:48,657 --> 01:00:49,783
Anyway...

510
01:00:49,808 --> 01:00:51,385
Enough sharing.

511
01:00:51,827 --> 01:00:54,579
The clock is ticking.

512
01:00:55,055 --> 01:00:56,098
Tick tock.

513
01:00:56,123 --> 01:00:57,123
Tick tock.

514
01:00:59,126 --> 01:01:00,627
In a little while,

515
01:01:01,378 --> 01:01:03,714
you’ll lose your house.

516
01:01:04,887 --> 01:01:07,194
And you’ll go viral too.

517
01:01:10,345 --> 01:01:11,763
But it’s your choice.

518
01:01:12,681 --> 01:01:14,725
I’m just giving you an option.

519
01:01:15,434 --> 01:01:16,434
And since...

520
01:01:16,643 --> 01:01:18,270
I’m feeling generous,

521
01:01:19,035 --> 01:01:20,035
From

522
01:01:20,105 --> 01:01:22,107
two million.

523
01:01:22,524 --> 01:01:27,779
I’ll make it three million
as your down payment.

524
01:01:31,116 --> 01:01:32,449
I’ll wait for your call.

525
01:02:16,694 --> 01:02:23,982
I accept your deal.

526
01:02:46,316 --> 01:02:48,735
The floor area is 80 square meters,

527
01:02:48,944 --> 01:02:51,071
and the lot area is 120 square meters.

528
01:02:52,030 --> 01:02:55,450
It’s the perfect size for the
business you want to build.

529
01:02:55,659 --> 01:02:56,659
Betchay.

530
01:02:56,786 --> 01:02:57,786
Who is he?

531
01:02:58,245 --> 01:03:00,247
He’s buying this house, why?

532
01:03:00,597 --> 01:03:01,597
I’ll take it.

533
01:03:01,765 --> 01:03:03,433
Since we’ve already
agreed on the price,

534
01:03:03,458 --> 01:03:04,835
when do we sign the papers?

535
01:03:05,168 --> 01:03:06,419
Excuse me.

536
01:03:07,712 --> 01:03:10,173
Betchay and I already
have an agreement.

537
01:03:10,298 --> 01:03:12,801
I’m the one buying this property.

538
01:03:13,385 --> 01:03:15,428
So with all due respect,

539
01:03:15,887 --> 01:03:16,972
please leave.

540
01:03:17,097 --> 01:03:19,307
Elsie, you’re the one
who should leave.

541
01:03:20,392 --> 01:03:22,310
Betchay, we had a deal.

542
01:03:22,978 --> 01:03:25,230
Forget about our deal.

543
01:03:25,772 --> 01:03:27,983
Now get out!

544
01:03:29,522 --> 01:03:31,237
You get out of here!

545
01:03:32,237 --> 01:03:34,311
- Get out!
- You bastard!

546
01:03:37,993 --> 01:03:38,993
Don’t!

547
01:03:41,030 --> 01:03:42,282
Stop! Please don’t!

548
01:03:42,314 --> 01:03:44,516
Not the sewing machine!

549
01:03:44,541 --> 01:03:46,239
That’s enough!

550
01:03:46,264 --> 01:03:47,904
Next time, watch who you’re dealing with!

551
01:03:49,629 --> 01:03:51,131
Come on. That’s enough!

552
01:07:29,323 --> 01:07:30,575
Hello, Elsie?

553
01:07:31,621 --> 01:07:33,748
I’ll do what you want, Gigi.

554
01:07:34,317 --> 01:07:36,164
I’ll kill Joel.

555
01:08:04,884 --> 01:08:06,344
Hi, Elsie!

556
01:08:14,727 --> 01:08:17,397
I knew you were just
playing hard to get.

557
01:08:20,625 --> 01:08:22,043
Just tell me straight.

558
01:08:23,278 --> 01:08:24,863
How do I kill Joel?

559
01:08:26,322 --> 01:08:29,492
Since... you’re used to
handling needles anyway.

560
01:08:30,403 --> 01:08:31,863
Poison him...

561
01:08:32,208 --> 01:08:33,209
With this.

562
01:08:43,579 --> 01:08:46,457
Why are you looking for
someone else to do this?

563
01:08:46,968 --> 01:08:47,968
Well,

564
01:08:48,011 --> 01:08:49,929
I tried to poison him before.

565
01:08:50,807 --> 01:08:52,600
He got suspicious.

566
01:08:53,600 --> 01:08:55,602
So you became my next option.

567
01:08:57,937 --> 01:08:59,524
Didn’t you love Joel?

568
01:09:00,915 --> 01:09:02,417
He raised you like his own daughter.

569
01:09:02,442 --> 01:09:05,069
But he was never
a real husband to my mom.

570
01:09:07,989 --> 01:09:09,866
He let her die.

571
01:09:11,034 --> 01:09:12,034
Gigi,

572
01:09:12,202 --> 01:09:14,162
Joel isn’t that kind of person.

573
01:09:15,371 --> 01:09:17,874
Are you trying to
change my mind, Elsie?

574
01:09:18,499 --> 01:09:20,210
You might get frustrated.

575
01:09:21,548 --> 01:09:24,385
I’ll make Joel’s death look natural.

576
01:09:25,256 --> 01:09:28,885
None of our relatives will question it.
They’re all in the America.

577
01:09:30,720 --> 01:09:33,097
And I won’t allow an autopsy!

578
01:09:34,641 --> 01:09:37,018
So you’re safe, Elsie.

579
01:09:42,148 --> 01:09:44,651
Three million, as promised.

580
01:13:35,923 --> 01:13:37,717
Any news, Elsie?

581
01:14:19,938 --> 01:14:20,938
[gasps]

582
01:14:21,761 --> 01:14:23,304
Oh my god, Elsie!

583
01:14:23,721 --> 01:14:24,847
You made it!

584
01:14:28,081 --> 01:14:29,374
You did it!

585
01:14:32,897 --> 01:14:34,440
Elsie, you did it!

586
01:14:36,108 --> 01:14:37,777
Ms. Geneva Aguilar,

587
01:14:38,556 --> 01:14:40,892
you’re under arrest
for frustrated murder.

588
01:14:41,346 --> 01:14:43,049
You have the right to remain silent.

589
01:14:43,074 --> 01:14:46,410
Anything you say may be used against you
in any court in the Philippines.

590
01:14:46,786 --> 01:14:50,256
You have the right to choose
your own competent and independent lawyer.

591
01:14:50,473 --> 01:14:52,975
If you cannot afford one,

592
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:54,835
the government will provide one for you.

593
01:14:54,860 --> 01:14:56,904
Do you understand these rights?

594
01:14:57,797 --> 01:14:58,965
What’s this, Elsie?

595
01:15:07,348 --> 01:15:08,558
Nice try,

596
01:15:08,849 --> 01:15:10,101
my fake daughter!

597
01:15:11,924 --> 01:15:14,092
Joel already knows everything, Gigi.

598
01:15:17,775 --> 01:15:19,735
Gigi asked me for a favor.

599
01:15:21,821 --> 01:15:23,656
She wanted me to kill you.

600
01:15:25,199 --> 01:15:27,034
In exchange for three million.

601
01:15:28,695 --> 01:15:29,712
Joel...

602
01:15:29,787 --> 01:15:32,748
She also blackmailed me
with the videos I sent you.

603
01:15:34,125 --> 01:15:35,876
She got into your phone.

604
01:15:40,881 --> 01:15:43,509
I’ve been wanting to
tell you this for days.

605
01:15:44,802 --> 01:15:46,429
She’s shameless.

606
01:15:48,306 --> 01:15:49,765
My own daughter?

607
01:15:50,349 --> 01:15:52,101
She’s not your daughter, Joel!

608
01:15:55,771 --> 01:15:57,398
She admitted it to me herself.

609
01:15:59,817 --> 01:16:02,486
That’s why she’s so
desperate to get your money.

610
01:16:09,827 --> 01:16:11,454
What did you two talk about?

611
01:16:21,964 --> 01:16:23,090
Did you get it on video?

612
01:16:29,221 --> 01:16:30,941
There’s no way she
can get out of this now?

613
01:16:37,148 --> 01:16:39,671
Thank you for telling me everything, Elsie.

614
01:16:48,532 --> 01:16:49,700
You bitch!

615
01:16:49,992 --> 01:16:51,160
- You shameless bitch!
- Gigi!

616
01:16:51,494 --> 01:16:52,726
- You bitch!
- Gigi!

617
01:16:52,912 --> 01:16:53,912
Enough!

618
01:16:58,751 --> 01:17:00,419
Dad, I’m sorry!

619
01:17:00,961 --> 01:17:04,048
- No!
- Every single

620
01:17:04,048 --> 01:17:06,550
police officer saw what you did, Gigi.

621
01:17:06,550 --> 01:17:08,636
I’m sorry!

622
01:17:09,345 --> 01:17:11,055
Dad, I’m sorry! No!

623
01:17:11,055 --> 01:17:12,056
Don’t call me Dad!

624
01:17:13,455 --> 01:17:14,935
- I'm sorry!
- You’re not my daughter!

625
01:17:15,768 --> 01:17:17,186
Dad, no!

626
01:17:17,186 --> 01:17:18,572
I’m sorry, Dad!

627
01:17:19,146 --> 01:17:20,398
Dad, I’m sorry!

628
01:17:20,423 --> 01:17:21,423
Now...

629
01:17:21,774 --> 01:17:24,026
I finally understand why...

630
01:17:24,819 --> 01:17:27,530
I could never feel close to you.

631
01:17:28,357 --> 01:17:30,366
No! Dad, don’t say that!

632
01:17:30,391 --> 01:17:32,059
No, Dad please!

633
01:17:33,452 --> 01:17:35,246
Do you know what hurts the most?

634
01:17:35,705 --> 01:17:36,705
Huh?

635
01:17:38,874 --> 01:17:40,126
I was good to you,

636
01:17:40,151 --> 01:17:42,570
but you were never good to me!

637
01:17:43,879 --> 01:17:44,879
And now...

638
01:17:46,173 --> 01:17:48,843
- Dad, no!
- You’ll pay for everything...

639
01:17:48,868 --> 01:17:51,410
- No, dad, please!
- you’ve done in prison.

640
01:17:51,435 --> 01:17:52,435
Dad!

641
01:17:52,805 --> 01:17:54,836
No!

642
01:17:55,099 --> 01:17:56,475
Dad, no!

643
01:17:56,500 --> 01:17:59,056
- You’ll pay for all of it!
- No! Dad!

644
01:17:59,395 --> 01:18:01,203
- Go.
- Dad, please!

645
01:18:01,230 --> 01:18:03,440
- Take her away.
- Dad! No!

646
01:18:03,482 --> 01:18:05,188
You bitch, Elsie!

647
01:18:05,276 --> 01:18:07,611
Dad, no please, no!

648
01:18:08,376 --> 01:18:09,376
No! Dad!

649
01:18:10,114 --> 01:18:12,415
- Dad, no please!
- Come with us.

650
01:18:12,533 --> 01:18:14,135
Please!

651
01:18:25,421 --> 01:18:26,922
Thank you so much, Elsie.

652
01:18:31,135 --> 01:18:33,804
You can finally live in peace, Joel.

653
01:18:37,372 --> 01:18:39,082
We can finally live in peace.

654
01:18:40,411 --> 01:18:42,621
Betchay won’t bother you anymore,

655
01:18:42,646 --> 01:18:45,900
because this house
and lot are finally yours.

656
01:18:48,353 --> 01:18:52,361
I even outbid the other buyer

657
01:18:52,531 --> 01:18:53,991
to make sure

658
01:18:55,034 --> 01:18:57,036
no one else could take it from you.

659
01:18:58,287 --> 01:18:59,371
Thank you...

660
01:18:59,538 --> 01:19:01,707
Thank you so, so much, Joel.

661
01:19:03,292 --> 01:19:04,502
I love you so much.

662
01:19:06,080 --> 01:19:08,214
I love you too, Joel.

663
01:19:17,556 --> 01:19:18,556
Now...

664
01:19:21,227 --> 01:19:22,812
Are you ready

665
01:19:24,021 --> 01:19:26,565
to become Mrs. Joel Aguilar?

666
01:19:28,132 --> 01:19:29,412
I’ve been ready for a long time.

667
01:19:30,361 --> 01:19:32,363
Ever since I first took your measurements.

668
01:19:34,365 --> 01:19:38,494
So you’ve wanted me since then?

669
01:19:39,620 --> 01:19:40,788
You’re so full of yourself!

670
01:19:44,291 --> 01:19:46,710
Are you excited for our honeymoon?

671
01:19:47,336 --> 01:19:48,337
Right away?

672
01:19:50,297 --> 01:19:51,423
Well...

673
01:19:52,132 --> 01:19:53,509
Let’s get married first.

674
01:19:54,468 --> 01:19:55,970
Will you marry me?

675
01:19:57,721 --> 01:19:59,181
Of course I will.
